description: Dex connector repository architecture and authoring rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dex Connectors Library

- Keep the Go SDK in sdkgo; keep every connector in its own Go module.
- Group one company's connectors under one directory. The first directory
  under connectors/ is the company, must match metadata.company, and must
  contain logo.svg.
- Keep provider calls in Dex Step Execute; never call providers from RPCs.
- Register every Attribute and Stream in the consuming Flow schema.
- Keep secrets out of durable state, Results, receipts, Streams, logs, generated
  values, and release artifacts.
- Treat connector.yaml as the source for company, release version, and
  generated connector APIs.
- Prefer operation-specific factories; generic Query/Mutation factories are
  advanced escape hatches.
- Every connector needs its own go.mod, README, manifest, generated code, and
  provider tests.
- Register every connector in the sorted root connectors.yaml list. Paths may
  have any depth below connectors/.
- Before changing Connector Step options, branches, retry, durability, or other
  Dex semantics, load the installed dex-developer skill. Cursor uses the
  dex-developer skill, Codex uses `$dex-developer`, and Claude Code uses
  `/dex:dex-developer`. If it is unavailable, stop and follow
  https://docs.superdurable.io/build-with-ai/dex-developer-skill.
- Only a happy-path branch is required. Mark every other branch `optional: true`.
  An unwired optional branch fails the Flow when selected. Mark a non-happy-path
  branch required only when the application must choose a different continuation,
  and say why in the branch description.
- Execute durability defaults to async. Use sync only when the operation is very
  likely to exceed 7 seconds, matching the Dex ASYNC local-activity limit. An LLM
  generation call can use sync. Do not choose sync because the timeout ceiling
  is 30 seconds.
